; One-man tank. See tank.gd: it drives itself once someone is aboard, and the
; hull stays put as permanent cover once it is knocked out.
;
; The turret is its own node so it can traverse independently of the hull, and
; so it can be thrown clear when the thing goes up. The gun pitches inside it,
; and both muzzles hang off the gun so they follow the barrel.
;
; Shaped after an M4A3E8: sponsons overhanging the tracks, a cast round turret
; with a rear bustle, six road wheels a side between a raised front sprocket and
; a rear idler, and a muzzle brake. No roof machine gun -- only the coax beside
; the main gun.
